# Adalimumab for rheumatoid arthritis, from the Utah Medicaid pharmacy prior authorization form for Humira (adalimumab)
# and biosimilars (last updated 4-1-26): Part I and section 7. Status draft: awaiting clinical sign-off (vaglio signoff).
# Every clause is quoted from library/sources/UT-Medicaid-adalimumab.txt. The sourced counterpart of the illustrative
# policies/adalimumab_ra.vaglio.
#
# Drafted by hand. Step therapy: an adequate trial of at least one DMARD for at least 3 months, or a contraindication to
# all. In the record, a trial is 90 days of one of the four DMARDs the form names, dispensed or taken, with no window (the
# form gives none); days of different drugs are not added together, since three months of one drug is the criterion.
# "Trial and failure" needs the failure too, which a dispense cannot show: so a record trial counts only beside the
# answered question that it failed (dmard_failed), and the question alone (dmard_trial_failed) is enough. The form's
# "if clinically appropriate" is left to review. The preferred-product question (Part I, 1) is formulary, not medical
# necessity, and is not encoded. Codes are from RxNav and the NLM HCPCS table, listed in the source with their origin.
policy adalimumab_ra_ut
  title "Adalimumab for rheumatoid arthritis (Utah Medicaid criteria)"
  version 0.1.0
  source "Utah Medicaid Pharmacy Prior Authorization Request Form, Humira (adalimumab) and Biosimilars, last updated 4-1-26, Part I and Part II section 7"
  status draft
  authority state
  lines medicaid
  states UT
  drug
  questionnaire https://vaglio.example/Questionnaire/adalimumab-ra-ut
  service hcpcs J0135
  service rxnorm 327361

evidence specialist
  text "Prescribed by or with a specialist in the disease"
  clause "Is the medication being prescribed by or in consultation with a provider specializing in the disease treatment?"
  find question specialist

evidence fda_use
  text "FDA-approved age, dosing, monitoring and contraindications are followed"
  clause "Does the requested medication and diagnosis follow FDA-approved age, dosing, monitoring and contraindications?"
  find question fda-use

evidence no_concurrent_biologic
  text "No concurrent TNF inhibitor, biologic, JAK inhibitor or PDE4 inhibitor"
  clause "Does the provider attest that the patient is not taking concurrent treatment or that the medication will not be used in combination with other TNF-inhibitors, biologic response modifiers or other biologic DMARDs, Janus kinase Inhibitors, or Phosphodiesterase 4 inhibitors (i.e., apremilast, tofacitinib, baricitinib) as verified by prescriber attestation, patient medication fill history, or submitted documentation?"
  find question no-concurrent-biologic

evidence adult
  text "18 years of age or older"
  clause "Is the patient at least 18 years of age or older?"
  find question adult

evidence active_ra
  text "Moderately to severely active rheumatoid arthritis, with baseline symptoms in the chart notes"
  clause "Does the patient have a diagnosis of moderately to severely active rheumatoid arthritis demonstrated by description of baseline symptoms present in the chart notes?"
  find question active-ra
  request document loinc 11506-3

evidence dmard_trial_failed
  text "An adequate trial and failure of a DMARD for at least 3 months"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find question dmard-trial-failed

evidence dmard_failed
  text "The DMARD tried did not control the disease"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find question dmard-failed

evidence methotrexate_90
  text "At least 90 days of methotrexate"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find medication rxnorm 6851 105585 105586 283510 283511 283671 lasting 90 days

evidence hydroxychloroquine_90
  text "At least 90 days of hydroxychloroquine"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find medication rxnorm 5521 979092 1119312 2569281 2569283 lasting 90 days

evidence leflunomide_90
  text "At least 90 days of leflunomide"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find medication rxnorm 27169 205284 205285 205286 lasting 90 days

evidence sulfasalazine_90
  text "At least 90 days of sulfasalazine"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find medication rxnorm 9524 198232 313142 lasting 90 days

evidence dmards_contraindicated
  text "A contraindication to all the DMARDs"
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  find question dmards-contraindicated

criterion no_specialist
  text "A specialist is not involved."
  clause "Is the medication being prescribed by or in consultation with a provider specializing in the disease treatment?"
  defeated by specialist

criterion not_fda_use
  text "FDA-approved use is not documented."
  clause "Does the requested medication and diagnosis follow FDA-approved age, dosing, monitoring and contraindications?"
  defeated by fda_use

criterion concurrent_unattested
  text "That no other biologic or targeted drug is taken with it is not attested."
  clause "Does the provider attest that the patient is not taking concurrent treatment or that the medication will not be used in combination with other TNF-inhibitors, biologic response modifiers or other biologic DMARDs, Janus kinase Inhibitors, or Phosphodiesterase 4 inhibitors (i.e., apremilast, tofacitinib, baricitinib) as verified by prescriber attestation, patient medication fill history, or submitted documentation?"
  defeated by no_concurrent_biologic

criterion not_adult
  text "The patient is not shown to be 18 or older."
  clause "Is the patient at least 18 years of age or older?"
  defeated by adult

criterion ra_unestablished
  text "Moderately to severely active rheumatoid arthritis is not documented."
  clause "Does the patient have a diagnosis of moderately to severely active rheumatoid arthritis demonstrated by description of baseline symptoms present in the chart notes?"
  defeated by active_ra

criterion no_record_trial
  text "No 90-day DMARD trial is in the record."
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  defeated by methotrexate_90 hydroxychloroquine_90 leflunomide_90 sulfasalazine_90

criterion failure_unstated
  text "That the DMARD failed is not stated."
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  defeated by dmard_failed

criterion record_trial_failed
  text "A 90-day DMARD trial in the record, which failed."
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  defeated by no_record_trial failure_unstated

criterion step_therapy_unmet
  text "No failed 3-month DMARD trial, and no contraindication to all DMARDs."
  clause "Has the patient had an adequate trial and failure of at least ONE disease modifying antirheumatic drug (DMARD) for at least 3 months (e.g. hydroxychloroquine, leflunomide, methotrexate, sulfasalazine) or a contraindication to all, if clinically appropriate?"
  defeated by dmard_trial_failed record_trial_failed dmards_contraindicated

criterion general_criteria_met
  text "The Part I criteria are met."
  clause "PART I: Criteria for Approval: (All of the following criteria must be met)"
  defeated by no_specialist not_fda_use concurrent_unattested

criterion ra_criteria_met
  text "The rheumatoid arthritis criteria are met."
  clause "Section 7: Additional criteria for Rheumatoid Arthritis (RA) (All of the following criteria must be met)"
  defeated by not_adult ra_unestablished step_therapy_unmet

decision approve approves
  text "Approve adalimumab."
  clause "PART I: Criteria for Approval: (All of the following criteria must be met)"
  defeated by no_specialist not_fda_use concurrent_unattested not_adult ra_unestablished step_therapy_unmet

decision deny_general denies
  text "Deny: a Part I criterion is not met (specialist, FDA-approved use, or no concurrent biologic)."
  clause "PART I: Criteria for Approval: (All of the following criteria must be met)"
  defeated by general_criteria_met

decision deny_ra denies
  text "Deny: a rheumatoid arthritis criterion is not met (age, active disease, or a failed 3-month DMARD trial)."
  clause "Section 7: Additional criteria for Rheumatoid Arthritis (RA) (All of the following criteria must be met)"
  defeated by ra_criteria_met
